BITSDIR="$(dirname "$0")"

# An install that brings its own runtime (bits.bits: /cvmfs/bits.cern.ch/bits)
# has it in runtime/ beside these scripts, and bits then runs its Python and its
# modulecmd from there by path, adding nothing to the environment of what it
# builds or loads. Otherwise (a git checkout, a pip install) BITS_PY is empty and
# python3, bitsBuild and modulecmd come from PATH exactly as before.
# That Python ignores the PYTHON* variables and the user's site-packages (-E -s):
# inside an entered environment they belong to the stack's Python, not to bits'.
BITS_PY=
[[ -x "$BITSDIR/runtime/bin/python3" ]] && BITS_PY="$BITSDIR/runtime/bin/python3"

function printHelp() {
  # The commands, by group. Every command gives its own help with --help.
  cat <<'EoF'
bits: build, publish and use software stacks.

Usage: bits [--community NAME] COMMAND [OPTIONS]
       bits help [COMMAND...]       the same as: bits COMMAND... --help
       bits --version

  --community NAME   first, for every command: the community ($BITS_COMMUNITY)
  -h, --help         this help; after a command, that command's help
  -d, --debug        debug output; not for the module commands, cvmfs, store,
                     use, overlay and preload

Using software (bits enter --help: their options, e.g. -a ARCH, -w DIR):
  q, query [REGEXP]       list the modules: local builds, then the community's
  enter MODULES           open a shell with MODULES loaded
  setenv MODULES -c CMD   run CMD with MODULES loaded
  load, printenv MODULES  print the shell code loading MODULES (to eval)
  unload MODULES          print the shell code unloading MODULES (to eval)
  list, avail             the loaded modules; all modules
  modulecmd ARGS          run modulecmd with ARGS
  shell-helper            a bits shell function for your shell startup file

Building:
  build PACKAGE           build a package and its dependencies
  status PACKAGE          what bits build would do
  deps PACKAGE            the dependency graph
  doctor [PACKAGE]        check this machine (and the recipes) for a build
  init [PACKAGE]          check out PACKAGE to develop it here
  use [SECTION] ARGS      save options for the commands run in this directory
  checksums               check (--write: record) a repository's checksums
  stats                   the resource report of a monitored build
  brew                    a Homebrew Brewfile from the recipes (macOS)
  clean                   remove temporary build trees and unused versions
  prune                   evict old packages from a persistent work directory
  architecture, version   the detected architecture; the bits version

CVMFS:
  cvmfs SUBCOMMAND        a deployed tree (platforms, show, summary), or
                          publishing a build (stage, publish, release)
  publish [PACKAGE]       publish packages of the work directory
  cvmfs-path              where a package is published
  import                  a foreign CVMFS deployment as a reuse overlay
  overlay FORMAT          the built packages in another format (e.g. lcg)
  preload                 CVMFS prefetch files for deployed packages

Trust and compliance:
  certify                 make a build trusted (passkey approval)
  sign                    sign the common manifest (manifests CI)
  verify                  check a deployment against its build manifest
  sbom                    a build manifest as an SBOM (CycloneDX, SPDX)
  trace FILE              who built, published and approved a file on CVMFS
